// Formative practice quiz for pull-requests-and-review. Low-stakes; answers are visible by design.
$CATEGORY: git-linux-ai-foundations/git-foundations/pull-requests-and-review

::pull-requests-and-review o1 - what a pull request asks::You open a pull request with base main and head feature/search. What does it ask for?{
=To merge feature/search into main after review#Correct. A pull request asks to merge the head branch into the base branch once teammates have reviewed it.
~To merge main into feature/search#Not quite. The direction runs from head to base, so feature/search goes into main.
~For teammates to pull feature/search onto their own laptops#Not quite. Despite the name, a pull request is about merging into the base branch, not about git pull.
~To merge feature/search into main immediately, with review optional#Not quite. The point of a pull request is that the change is reviewed before it is merged.
}

::pull-requests-and-review o2 - the fix does not show::A reviewer commented on PR \#30. You fixed it and committed on the same branch, but the PR on GitHub does not show your fix. Why?{
=You have not pushed the branch yet#Correct. The PR shows the branch as it is on GitHub. git push uploads your commit, and the PR updates itself.
~Fixes must go in a new pull request#Not quite. You answer a review on the same branch; the existing PR picks up new commits after you push.
~You must reply to the comment before the commit can appear#Not quite. Replying is good practice, but only a push makes the commit appear.
~You should have committed the fix on main#Not quite. The fix belongs on the PR's head branch, so it is reviewed before reaching main.
}

::pull-requests-and-review o3 - an AI-made pull request::An AI coding assistant opened a pull request. All required checks pass, but no person has reviewed it yet. Should it be merged?{
=No. It still needs a reviewer's approval and resolved comments; AI-made changes get the same review and more#Correct. Passing checks is one of three conditions. Approval and resolved comments are also required.
~Yes. Passing checks prove the change is correct#Not quite. Checks catch only what they test. A merge also needs reviewer approval and resolved comments.
~Yes. Changes written by AI do not need human review#Not quite. AI-made changes need at least as careful a review as any other change.
~Yes, as long as the change is small#Not quite. Size does not remove the need for approval, passing checks and resolved comments.
}

::pull-requests-and-review o3 - a pending required check::A pull request has two approvals and every comment is resolved, but a required lint check is still running. Should it be merged now?{
=Not yet. Wait until the required check passes#Correct. A merge needs approval, passing required checks and resolved comments, all three. A running check has not passed yet.
~Yes. Two approvals override the checks#Not quite. Approvals and checks are separate conditions; both must be met.
~Yes. A check that is still running counts as passing#Not quite. Only a finished, successful check counts as passing.
~No. Open a new pull request so the check runs again#Not quite. The check is already running on this PR. Wait for it to finish.
}
